    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **47 tests, 0 failures**, including the new `Cp34Tests` and all pre-existing tests.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe feature is a read-derived field on the `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow, so I followed the same pattern the codebase already uses for `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, etc. (a stored input + a mapper-computed derived value):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (DTO source of truth)\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (ISO date) to `OwnerFields` (the request/response fields).\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` to `Owner` (the response schema).\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `birthDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a new `birth_date DATE` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct binds `birthDate` request\u2192entity and entity\u2192response by name automatically.\n\n3. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql); tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`AgeBands` helper** (`rest/function/common/`) \u2014 computes the band from `birthDate` measured against the owner's stored `registrationDate` (falling back to today only if absent): `MINOR` under 18, `ADULT` 18\u201364, `SENIOR` 65+; returns `null` when no birth date is on record (so the field is simply absent).\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 registered `AgeBands` in `imports` and added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = \"java(AgeBands.of(owner))\")`.\n\nBecause `ageBand` is derived in the mapper from the stored `birthDate` and the (already business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, it comes out consistently on both the create response and later reads without touching the OfficeFloor pipeline.",
